<task id="027" project="spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>FR-10: open the related record and the Document record from the pane</title>
    <phase>2 Save flow</phase>
    <gate>003+026 complete</gate>
    <status>not-started</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Modifies .tsx/.ts client code, introduces a host-integration mechanism (Office Dialog API) with an auth boundary, and touches the BFF read surface; tags include frontend + office-addins.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Spike-2 has already resolved the mechanism question by the time this runs; the task implements the chosen branch against a documented fallback. The ADR-050 tension is pre-resolved as Path C.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>P2-b</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>003,026</deps>
    <tags>frontend, fluent-ui, office-addins, bff-api, e2e-test</tags>
    <estimated-effort>1 day</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>Make the related-record card (task 026) and a Document-record affordance actually open their records from the pane, using the mechanism Spike-2 (task 003) determined. The preferred mechanism is the Office Dialog API; if the spike came back negative, implement the documented fallback instead — read-only detail in-pane with a browser-tab escape hatch. Record which branch was taken in `notes/`.</prompt>

  <role>SPAARKE platform developer. Expertise in the Office Dialog API (dialog lifecycle, `messageParent`, framing constraints), Office add-in auth context, and Fluent UI v9. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>

  <goal>From the pane, a user can open the related record and the `sprk_document` record, use them, and see any change they made reflected in the pane on return. The mechanism matches Spike-2's finding; whichever branch was taken is recorded with its rationale in `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/`.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      spec.md FR-10: open the related record and the `sprk_document` record from the pane. Preferred mechanism is the Office Dialog API (see Spike-2). Acceptance: the record opens and is usable, and edits made there are reflected in the pane on return.

      Spike-2 (task 003) answers four questions and gates this task: (a) can the Office Dialog host an MDA record form without a framing refusal, or must we host a Spaarke code page? (b) does auth context travel via `messageParent`? (c) does the form function at dialog size? (d) does a change propagate back to the pane?

      ADR TENSION — ALREADY RESOLVED, do not re-litigate. spec.md ADR Tensions records ADR-050 as PATH C: the Office dialog is host chrome and sits outside ADR-050's scope, so `SprkModal` cannot and need not wrap it. BUT any Spaarke UI rendered INSIDE the dialog still follows ADR-050 and ADR-021. Cite this resolution in the PR rather than reopening it.

      The documented fallback, if Spike-2 is negative: read-only detail in-pane with a browser-tab escape hatch. That is an acceptable outcome for this task — write the implementation so either branch satisfies the acceptance criteria, and record the choice.

      Verified constraint: `Xrm.*` does NOT exist in an Office host (NFR-03). Any deep-link or navigation must be constructed from configuration, not from `Xrm.Navigation`. The add-in already reads an `ORG_URL` environment variable for the Quick-Create deep link, with an unset value being a safe no-op — follow that precedent rather than hardcoding an org URL.

      Task 026 exposes the click seam on the related-record card. This task fills it and adds the equivalent affordance for the `sprk_document` record itself.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file role="canonical-reference">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/spikes/spike-2-dialog-api.md</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/RelatedRecordCard.tsx</file>
      <file role="new">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/openRecordLauncher.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/adapters/IHostAdapter.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/adapters/WordAdapter.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/adapters/OutlookAdapter.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/SaveFlow.tsx</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/createTodoLauncher.ts</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">src/client/office-addins/shared/services/AuthService.ts</file>
      <file role="modify">tests/integration/contract/Api/Office/OfficeEndpointsContractTests.cs</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="003" status="pending">Spike-2 — determines the record-open mechanism: Office Dialog hosting an MDA form, Office Dialog hosting a Spaarke code page, or the documented in-pane fallback.</dependency>
      <dependency task="026" status="pending">FR-09 related-record card — exposes the click seam this task fills and names the record to open.</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — read `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/spikes/spike-2-dialog-api.md` FIRST and implement the branch it selected. BOTH the Office Dialog path and the documented fallback (read-only detail in-pane plus a browser-tab escape hatch) are acceptable outcomes for this task. Record the branch taken and its rationale in `projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-050">SCOPE — resolved as PATH C for this project: the Office dialog is host chrome, outside ADR-050's scope, so it is NOT wrapped in `SprkModal`. However, any Spaarke-rendered UI INSIDE the dialog (and any in-pane fallback detail view) still follows ADR-050 and ADR-021. Cite this resolution in the PR; do not re-litigate the tension.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-021">SCOPE — for every surface this task renders (dialog contents, in-pane fallback, the open affordances themselves): Fluent UI v9 semantic tokens only, no hex literals; honors the Office light/dark theme via `useOfficeTheme`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-03: `Xrm.*` does not exist in an Office host. MUST NOT call `Xrm.Navigation`, MUST NOT import any Xrm-bound component, and MUST NOT assume a model-driven app JS context inside the dialog.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — no hardcoded org URLs. Any record deep link is built from configuration, following the existing `ORG_URL` precedent where an unset value is a safe no-op rather than a broken link.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028">SCOPE — auth for anything the dialog loads uses NAA via `@spaarke/auth` `OfficeNaaStrategy`, wrapped by `shared/services/AuthService.ts`. MUST NOT construct MSAL directly in this package (arch-test enforced), and MUST NOT pass a raw access token through `messageParent` or a query string.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — NFR-10 shared-first: the launcher lands in `shared/taskpane/` and is gated by `hostAdapter.getCapabilities()`, not by a `hostType === 'word'` conditional inside a view. If a host cannot open a dialog, the capability reports false and the fallback renders.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-012">SCOPE — for this add-in package only: per this project's Path A exception, any in-pane detail view is a thin view under `shared/taskpane/`. MUST NOT import `@spaarke/ui-components`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the return path: an edit made in the opened record MUST be reflected in the pane on return. Whether that is driven by a `messageParent` message, a dialog-close event, or a re-read on focus, the mechanism must be explicit and tested, not left to chance.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-044">SCOPE — every record GUID used to build a link or a dialog URL MUST be canonicalized bare-lowercase via `cleanGuid` before use.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">SCOPE — any endpoint this task adds or modifies gets a contract test. The record-open behavior itself gets end-to-end coverage per the ui-tests block below. Cite `docs/adr/ADR-038-testing-strategy.md` — there is no concise copy in `.claude/adr/`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — BFF publish size: measure the delta against a FRESH BUILD OF `origin/master`, never against the recorded baseline number (root CLAUDE.md §10 bullet 4). Zip both with PowerShell `Compress-Archive` and report both absolute sizes, the delta, and the tool name. If this task turns out to be client-only, state that explicitly and record a zero-delta measurement rather than skipping it.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — the PR description MUST state the Placement Justification for any BFF-side change per `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — run `/conflict-check` before opening any BFF-touching PR. `spaarkeai-compose-r8` and `unified-access-control-r2` are live on the same hot path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project">SCOPE — build commands for `src/client/office-addins` only: install with `npm install --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund`; there is NO `build:prod` script — `npm run build` IS the production build.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
    <topic>Office Dialog API, add-in auth context, record deep-linking without Xrm</topic>
