    <patterns>
      <pattern name="fluent-v9-host-visual-fit" location=".claude/patterns/ui/fluent-v9-host-visual-fit.md">Explicitly covers Office add-ins. Governs both the open affordance in the narrow pane and any Spaarke UI rendered inside the dialog.</pattern>
      <pattern name="spaarke-sso-binding" location=".claude/patterns/auth/spaarke-sso-binding.md">INV-1..INV-8. Read before deciding how auth reaches whatever the dialog loads; a token must never travel in a URL or a `messageParent` payload.</pattern>
    </patterns>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Load projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/CLAUDE.md, spec.md FR-10 and its ADR Tensions row (ADR-050 Path C), and the knowledge files above. Output the mandatory rigor declaration (FULL) per root CLAUDE.md §8.</step>
    <step order="1">Read `notes/spikes/spike-2-dialog-api.md` and restate its four answers (framing, auth, dialog-size usability, change propagation) in the task log. Choose the branch it selected. If the file does not exist, this task is not startable — stop and report that task 003 has not closed.</step>
    <step order="2">Add an `canOpenRecord`-style capability to `IHostAdapter` and implement it in both `WordAdapter` and `OutlookAdapter`, so the view gates on capability rather than host type (NFR-10).</step>
    <step order="3">Build `openRecordLauncher.ts` in `shared/taskpane/services/`, following the shape of the existing `createTodoLauncher.ts`. It takes a canonicalized record reference and opens it via the chosen mechanism, exposing a completion/return signal.</step>
    <step order="4">Wire the launcher into the related-record card's click seam from task 026, and add an equivalent affordance for the `sprk_document` record itself.</step>
    <step order="5">Implement the return path: on dialog close or on the propagation signal Spike-2 identified, re-read the affected pane state (profile, record card) so edits made in the record are visible without a manual refresh.</step>
    <step order="6">If the fallback branch was taken: build the read-only in-pane detail view plus a browser-tab escape hatch, and make the return path a re-read on focus. Same acceptance criteria apply.</step>
    <step order="7">Add unit tests: capability gating, launcher invocation with a canonicalized GUID, the return-path re-read, and the no-capability fallback rendering.</step>
    <step order="8">Run `npm run typecheck`, `npm test`, `npm run build`; if any BFF file changed, run `dotnet build` and the Office contract tests. All green.</step>
    <step order="9">Measure BFF publish size against a fresh `origin/master` build per the constraint above, or record an explicit zero-delta if this task is client-only.</step>
    <step order="10">Run `/conflict-check` if any BFF file changed, then code-review + adr-check per task-execute Step 9.5.</step>
    <step order="11">Record the branch taken (dialog or fallback) and its rationale in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/027-record-open-mechanism.md.</step>
    <step order="12">Update tasks/TASK-INDEX.md: set this task's status to ✅.</step>
    <step order="13">Document any deviation in projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/.</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>If implementing the chosen branch would require passing an access token through a URL, a query string, or a `messageParent` payload, STOP and escalate per CLAUDE.md §6 — that violates ADR-028 and the `spaarke-sso-binding` invariants, and no dialog convenience justifies it.</trigger>
    <trigger>If Spike-2's finding no longer holds when you exercise it (for example the dialog now refuses framing where the spike said it did not), STOP and escalate rather than silently switching branches — the spike is the project's recorded evidence and a contradiction needs to be reconciled, not overwritten.</trigger>
    <trigger>If the change-propagation requirement ("edits made there are reflected in the pane on return") cannot be met by either branch, STOP and escalate — that is an acceptance criterion in spec.md FR-10, not a nice-to-have to drop quietly.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>Closest neighbor: `src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/createTodoLauncher.ts` — the existing "launch something from the pane" service, with tests at `services/__tests__/createTodoLauncher.test.ts`. Grep run over `src/client/office-addins` for `displayDialogAsync`, `messageParent`, and `openRecord` returns nothing: no record-open mechanism exists in this package today. `Xrm.Navigation` is unavailable here by NFR-03, so there is no platform launcher to call either.</existing>
    <extension>No. `createTodoLauncher` launches a create-form flow with a To Do payload and owns that payload's shape; the record-open launcher takes an arbitrary record reference and owns a dialog/return lifecycle instead. They share no state and change for different reasons. The launcher does reuse `createTodoLauncher`'s SHAPE and its capability-gating discipline rather than inventing a new one.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>Without it, the related-record card (task 026) is a dead label: the user can see which matter a document is filed to but cannot reach it, and the pane's profile fields — which are read-only by design (FR-07 / spec Assumptions) — have no edit path at all. FR-13's "finish editing in the record" premise also has no mechanism behind it.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <ui-tests>
    <test name="Open the related record from the card">
      <steps>
        <step>Open a Spaarke-sourced Word document filed to a matter and view the Save tab.</step>
        <step>Click the related-record card.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The matter record opens via the mechanism Spike-2 selected and is usable — fields are readable and, in the dialog branch, editable at dialog size.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Open the Document record from the pane">
      <steps>
        <step>On the same identified document, use the Document-record affordance.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The `sprk_document` record opens and is usable.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Edits propagate back to the pane">
      <steps>
        <step>Open the Document record, change a field the pane displays (for example the document name or a profile field), and close the record.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>On return, the pane reflects the change without a manual refresh or a pane reload.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Capability gating, not host branching">
      <steps>
        <step>Run the pane in a host whose adapter reports the open-record capability as false.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>The fallback surface renders; no `hostType === 'word'` conditional appears in the view code (verified by grep during review).</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="ADR-021 dark-mode check via the Office theme toggle">
      <steps>
        <step>Switch the Office theme to Dark and reload the pane; view the open affordances, and any Spaarke UI rendered inside the dialog or in the fallback detail view.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Every Spaarke-rendered surface resolves its colors from Fluent v9 semantic tokens with legible contrast in dark mode; no hex literals; repeat in Light mode with the same result. Host chrome around the dialog is out of scope.</expected>
    </test>
    <test name="Keyboard-only operation (NFR-11)">
      <steps>
        <step>Using only the keyboard, reach and activate both open affordances, and return from the opened record.</step>
      </steps>
      <expected>Both affordances are reachable and operable by keyboard; focus returns sensibly to the pane on close; the return is announced via `useAnnounce`.</expected>
    </test>
  </ui-tests>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build the BFF and run the Office contract tests, if any BFF file changed.</tool>
    <tool name="npm">Install with --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund; typecheck, test, and build (build IS production here).</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/openRecordLauncher.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/adapters/IHostAdapter.ts</output>
    <output type="code">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/components/RelatedRecordCard.tsx</output>
    <output type="test">src/client/office-addins/shared/taskpane/services/__tests__/openRecordLauncher.test.ts</output>
    <output type="doc">projects/spaarkeai-word-add-in-r1/notes/027-record-open-mechanism.md</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Spike-2 report exists, when this task starts, then its four answers are restated in the task log and the selected branch is cited in the PR before any code is written.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an identified document with a related record, when the user activates the card, then the related record opens via the selected mechanism and is usable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an identified document, when the user activates the Document-record affordance, then the `sprk_document` record opens and is usable.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given an edit made in the opened record to a field the pane displays, when the user returns to the pane, then the pane reflects the change without a manual refresh.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Office Dialog branch, when reviewed, then the dialog itself is NOT wrapped in `SprkModal` (ADR-050 Path C) AND any Spaarke UI rendered inside it uses Fluent v9 semantic tokens per ADR-021.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the fallback branch, when reviewed, then a read-only in-pane detail view plus a browser-tab escape hatch is implemented, the return path re-reads pane state, and `notes/027-record-open-mechanism.md` records why the fallback was taken.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given a host whose adapter reports the open-record capability as false, when the pane renders, then the fallback surface appears and no host-type conditional exists in the view code.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: given no configured org URL, when the open affordance is activated, then it is a safe no-op with a stated reason rather than opening a broken link.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No access token appears in any URL, query string, or `messageParent` payload; no MSAL is constructed in this package; verified by grep and by the arch-test.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Every record GUID used to build a link or dialog URL is canonicalized via `cleanGuid`; verified by inspection during code review.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given the Office theme set to Dark, when every Spaarke-rendered surface added by this task is viewed, then all colors resolve from Fluent v9 semantic tokens and no hex literal appears in the added styles.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`npm run typecheck` is clean for the files this task touched; `npm test` and `npm run build` pass; if any BFF file changed, `dotnet build` and the Office contract tests pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Publish-size impact is either measured against a fresh `origin/master` build with `Compress-Archive` or explicitly recorded as zero-delta because the task is client-only.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    spec.md FR-10, its Owner Clarification ("Dialog API (a) preferred — investigate first; (c) is the documented fallback"), and its ADR Tensions row resolving ADR-050 as Path C; plan.md §4 Phase 2 task 027 and Unresolved Question on the Spike-2 outcome. Note that a negative Spike-2 also weakens FR-13's "finish editing in the record" premise — if the fallback branch is taken, say so in `notes/` so the Phase 3 creation-completeness tasks can account for it.
  </notes>

